{%- comment -%}
  The buyer's own painting as each gift's picture in Shopify's order emails (Settings, Notifications:
  Order confirmation, Shipping confirmation, Shipping update, Out for delivery, Delivered).
  Without it the email shows the product's variant picture, an example dog (Ruling, Krish, 2026-11-05: the
  variant pictures stay example dogs for the ads), so a buyer who painted their own dog sees a stranger's.
  Replace each block that starts `{% if <var>.image %}` and draws `<var> | img_url: 'compact_cropped'` with
  this whole file, then set hs_l on the first code line to that block's line item:
    - Order confirmation, plain lines: `line` (as below);
    - Order confirmation, lines inside a bundle group: `component`;
    - the four shipping emails loop over fulfillment lines, so the gift is `line.line_item`.
  A bundle group's own top picture is line-item-group-painting.liquid. Live in all five templates since
  10 Nov 2026 (docs/evidence/2026-11-10-fulfillment-and-thumbnails/REPORT.md).
  The picture comes from _hs_checkout_image (the checkout picture the cart registered), then
  _customization_image (Teeinblue's preview), then the variant picture. Tested by
  tools/preview/line-item-painting-email.test.mjs.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign hs_l = line -%}
{%- assign hs_line_img = hs_l.properties._hs_checkout_image | default: hs_l.properties._customization_image | default: '' -%}
{%- if hs_line_img != '' -%}
<img src="{{ hs_line_img }}" align="left" width="60" height="60" class="order-list__product-image" alt="{{ hs_l.title | escape }}">
{%- elsif hs_l.image -%}
<img src="{{ hs_l | img_url: 'compact_cropped' }}" align="left" width="60" height="60" class="order-list__product-image" alt="{{ hs_l.title | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}
